# A line with no newline after it ends in a ⊖: on the added row of a new file without one, and
# on the deleted row where a change gives a file the newline it lacked. Its help is a tooltip,
# which scripts can't show; the tests check what it says.
wait settled
open tamarinworks/gazette#273
wait settled

click image #doc
expect text "batch/status.go" in #file-header
expect textarea has value ~"} ⊖"
snap missing-newline-added textarea

click text "main.go"
wait until text "cmd/gazette/main.go" in #file-header
expect textarea has value ~"} ⊖"
snap missing-newline-restored textarea
